%description:

TcpVegas.beta:linux -- with more than 4 extra segments, the window shrinks by one segment for each round trip.

The claim (TcpVegas.ned): "in congestion avoidance, above this many extra segments, cwnd shrinks
by one segment for each RTT".

The classes: linux (4, the default, the value of Linux tcp_vegas.c), other (a larger value),
invalid (below alpha). The code: once
each round trip, TcpVegas::receivedAckForUnackedData() compares the extra segments, diff,
with the thresholds; TcpVegas::initializeAlgorithm() checks them. This test separates "linux" from "other".

Host under test: host1, with TcpVegas and gamma 30 (precondition: slow start ends at about 96
segments, 62 more than the path holds), which sends to host2; the path
is host1 -- tap -- router -- host2, with a bottleneck of 10 Mbps from the router to host2 and
a round trip of 40 ms, so the path holds 34 segments; host2 has no delayed ACK
(precondition: a delayed ACK makes the round trips longer than the queue does) and a window
of 1000000 bytes. Observation: level 3, at 3 s, the window is 75000 to 100000 bytes: after slow start it was
about 122640, and it lost one segment in each round trip of about 100 ms.

%# parameter: TcpVegas.beta
%# class: linux
%# value: 4
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.beta
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpVegasBetaLinux")
        .act(action().at(3.0)
                 .describe("the window at 3 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.snd_cwnd >= 75000 && state.snd_cwnd <= 100000"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpVegasBetaLinux compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.beta = 4    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpVegas"
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.linkDelay = 5ms
*.bottleneckDatarate = 10Mbps
*.bottleneckDelay = 10ms
*.host2.tcp.delayedAcksEnabled = false
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 1000000
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 10000000B
sim-time-limit = 3.5s
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.gamma = 30
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpVegasBetaLinux: PASS
